ENG-07  D3DMetal layer: V-Sync kept on, and a page that tells when each frame reached the screen.

dlls/winemac.drv/d3dmetal_objc.m (WineMetalLayer), macdrv_main.c (winemac.so). Lullaby, 2026-10-17
(commits 91cd3eb, cc2a16b). LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

What, both read once per process from the env files and off by default:
 LULLABY_FORCE_VSYNC=1  the layer stays in step with the display (games with frame generation switch
                        V-Sync off and tear); with it the layer keeps at least three drawables, so that a
                        frame waiting for a refresh does not starve the GPU of drawables.
 LULLABY_PRESENT_FEED=1 <prefix>/.sevo/run/<Windows pid>.present: every drawable handed out and the moment
                        it reached the screen (addPresentedHandler), a ring of 256 in a shared page
                        (magic "LBPRSENT"). lullaby-nvapi64.dll (patches/inject/lby-rainbowdash-reflex, Reflex by Lullaby) reads it.
Without the variables the patch changes nothing.
Requires: nothing in the patch; Reflex needs patches/inject/lby-rainbowdash-reflex (CMP-04).
Other bases: FAIL on every WineForge release; it patches Dormison's WineMetalLayer, WineForge's
d3dmetal_objc.m is different code. Needs rewriting for it; Reflex and V-Sync depend on it.
Test: make reflex-sim (the feed is simulated there); in a game, lullaby-nvapi.log.
Verified on: Dormison r7, built into bridge-dormison-r7-1 (2026-10-23), which the owner ran with RE9, PEAK and ETS2 (not each patch on its own).
Switch: LULLABY_FORCE_VSYNC=1 and LULLABY_PRESENT_FEED=1; both are off unless set (the game settings' V-Sync and Reflex switches set them).

